CORE
nested_call1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.r0 == 4'b1010: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.r1 == 4'b1100: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p2\] always main\.r2 == 4'b1000: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p3\] always \(##1 main\.q == 4'b1011\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p4\] always main\.r3 == 4'b0011: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p5\] always \(##1 main\.s1 == 4'b1000\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p6\] always \(##1 main\.s2 == 4'b0110\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p7\] always \(##1 main\.s3 == 4'b0101\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Calls of a function nested in calls of the same function, as arguments and
recursively, and functions and tasks called as statements. The bindings of
the parameters of an enclosing call must survive the expansion of the
nested call.
